      "code_path": "stem-bot-v2/src/utils/discord.ts::getMember::L47-58",
      "proof_trace": "The catch block at L54-57 returns null unconditionally for all error types — including 404 (not found), 429 (rate limit), and 5xx (server/network errors) — without inspecting error.status or error.code. This collapses two semantically distinct failure modes into a single null return, breaking the property. The most impactful consequence is in memberStatus.ts:L18-27, where a null from an API error causes the endpoint to respond with is_in_server: false, falsely reporting a valid member as absent from the server.",
      "attack_scenario": "If the Discord API becomes transiently unavailable (rate limit, network failure, or outage), calls to GET /api/member/status return is_in_server: false for legitimate members; any downstream access-control logic relying on this field would incorrectly deny or revoke access for those members.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-stem-bot-v21-inv-014"
    },
    "text": "getMember errors must distinguish not-found from API failure; not silently return null for both.",
    "assertion": "forall uid: getMember(uid) error => error_type in {NOT_FOUND, API_ERROR}, not null",
    "covers": "SG-017_discordGetMember",
    "severity": "LOW",
    "type": "invariant"
  }
}

